 "standard_text": "Solve problems on direct, inverse, joint and partial variation; find the constant of variation; write equations of variation. (summary of the NERDC JSS 3 Mathematics curriculum)",
 "meta_desc": "Free JSS 3 maths worksheets on variation: direct and inverse variation, the constant k, variation with squares and word problems. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "Direct: y = kx. Inverse: y = k/x",
 "key_sub": "Find k first.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>y varies directly as x: y = kx. If x is multiplied by 3, so is y.</li><li>y varies inversely as x: y = k ÷ x, so xy = k.</li><li>Always find the constant k from the given values first, then use it.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>y ∝ x, y = 12 when x = 3. Find y when x = 5</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>k = 4</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: y = 20</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Using direct variation when one quantity goes down</td><td>That is inverse.</td></tr><tr><td>Forgetting to find k</td><td>Find k from the first pair.</td></tr><tr><td>Squaring k instead of x</td><td>y = kx² squares x only.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
